## Why this licence

This workshop adapts material from open educational resources that are themselves
released under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. The ShareAlike condition propagates to derivative
works, so this repository carries the same terms:

- Pasha, I. & Agostino, C., *Python for Astronomers*
  https://prappleizer.github.io/
- Zingale, M., *Tutorial on Computational Astrophysics*
  https://zingale.github.io/comp_astro_tutorial/
- Rougier, N. P., *Scientific Visualization: Python + Matplotlib*
  https://github.com/rougier/scientific-visualization-book

Free educational use — student workshops, university courses, self-study — is
squarely within these terms. Paid training built on this material is not.

---

## What this licence does NOT cover

**Carroll, B. W. & Ostlie, D. A., *An Introduction to Modern Astrophysics*, 2nd ed.**
(Pearson Addison-Wesley, 2007) is a copyrighted commercial textbook and is **not**
covered by this licence. This repository cites section numbers, equation numbers and
problem numbers, and reimplements the physics in original code. It does not reproduce
the text, figures, or problem statements beyond brief attributed quotation. Readers
need their own copy.

**Gaia data** is provided by ESA under its own terms and carries a mandatory
acknowledgement requirement. See the README.

**Third-party Python packages** (astropy, numpy, scipy, matplotlib, scikit-learn,
astroquery) retain their own licences.
